    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\text{ m}$; the common factor $2x-3$ cancels, so the width is constant.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Width}&=\\frac{\\text{area}}{\\text{length}}\\\\&=\\frac{10x-15}{2x-3}\\\\&=\\frac{5(2x-3)}{2x-3}\\\\&=5\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe width is constant because the simplified expression does not depend on $x$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
